<title>USA: USDA releases $300 Mln in GSM-102 for Mexico.</title>
<headline>USDA releases $300 Mln in GSM-102 for Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday it released an additional $300 million in short-term export credit guarantees to Mexico.</p>
<p>With the release, $800 million of the $1.075 million earmarked for Mexico are available to exporters.  </p>
<p>Some $275 million remained to be allocated for fiscal 1997, the agency said.</p>
<p>USDA did not alter its list of products eligible for export credit guarantees under the short-term GSM-102 program. Terms of coverage were unchanged.</p>
</text>
